.Dd $Mdocdate$
.Dt EGGHEAD-SERVE 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm egghead-serve
.Nd run the web UI and MCP HTTP server
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm egghead serve
.Op Fl -port Ar n
.Op Fl -config Ar path
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Cm serve
starts a long-lived process that hosts the web UI, the records
browser, the chat-room UI, and the MCP HTTP endpoint at
.Pa /mcp ,
all on the same port. Logs are written to standard output. The
command runs in the foreground; it does not daemonize itself.
.Pp
The same supervision tree backs the TUI. If a
.Cm serve
process is already running on the same machine, launching the TUI
or any other
.Nm
command attaches to it as a client over BEAM distribution. Same-host
attach is zero-config; cross-host attach is documented in
.Xr egghead 5
under the
.Sy server:
section.
.Pp
For the MCP stdio transport, used by editor integrations,
see
.Xr egghead-mcp 1
instead.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width "--config path"
.It Fl -port Ar n
Override
.Sy web.port
from the configuration for this invocation. Default:
.Sy 4000 .
.It Fl -config Ar path
Override the configuration file location.
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Show help.
.El
.Sh BIND AND EXPOSURE
The default
.Sy web.bind
is
.Sy 127.0.0.1 .
.Nm
performs no authentication of its own; a network-reachable endpoint
without authentication exposes the entire records store and the
agent layer. There are two safe deployments: loopback only, and
loopback plus a reverse proxy that handles authentication and TLS.
Binding to
.Sy 0.0.0.0
is only safe when the network itself authenticates connections (a
tailnet, a private VPC, a LAN you trust). See
.Xr egghead 5
and the
.Sx Running a node
guide for the full discussion.
.Sh SHUTDOWN
The process exits cleanly on
.Sy SIGTERM
or with the BEAM break sequence
.Pq Sy Ctrl-C, then a .
.Pp
For unattended operation, install the user-scope service supervisor
with
.Xr egghead-service 1 ,
which writes a LaunchAgent on macOS or a systemd user unit on Linux,
restarts on failure, and routes logs to the standard XDG log file.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Run on the default port:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
egghead serve
.Ed
.Pp
Run on a custom port:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
egghead serve --port 8080
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr egghead-mcp 1 ,
.Xr egghead-service 1 ,
.Xr egghead-config 1 ,
.Xr egghead-doctor 1 ,
.Xr egghead-logs 1 ,
.Xr egghead 1 ,
.Xr egghead 5
